---
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>CLI Advanced - Semicons</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <nav>
        <a href="/semicons/" class="logo">Semicons</a>
        <a href="/semicons/docs/cli-quickstart">CLI</a>
        <div class="dropdown">
          <a href="/semicons/docs/framework/react-quickstart" class="dropdown-toggle">Framework</a>
          <div class="dropdown-menu">
            <a href="/semicons/docs/framework/react-quickstart">React</a>
            <a href="/semicons/docs/framework/vue-quickstart">Vue</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <article>
        <h1>CLI Advanced Usage</h1>
        <p>
          Learn about advanced CLI features including scanning, diagnostics, and strict mode.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2>Scan Command</h2>
          <p>
            The <code>scan</code> command analyzes your codebase for icon usage patterns and violations.
          </p>

          <h3>Basic Usage</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli scan ./src</code></pre>

          <h3>Options</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Option</th>
                <th>Description</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>-d, --dir &lt;path&gt;</code></td>
                <td>Directory to scan (default: current directory)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>-c, --config &lt;path&gt;</code></td>
                <td>Path to config file</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>-f, --format &lt;text|json|html&gt;</code></td>
                <td>Output format (default: text)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>--fail-on &lt;error|warn|never&gt;</code></td>
                <td>Exit condition (default: error)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <h3>Output Formats</h3>
          <p><strong>Text (default):</strong></p>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli scan ./src -f text

┌─────────┬────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬──────────┐
│ File    │ Line       │ Message                       │ Level    │
├─────────┼────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼──────────┤
│ App.tsx │ 15         │ Direct .svg import detected   │ error    │
│ Menu.tsx│ 23         │ Unknown token "foo:bar"       │ error    │
└─────────┴────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴──────────┘
[scan] Found 2 violations</code></pre>

          <p><strong>JSON:</strong></p>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli scan ./src -f json</code></pre>

          <h3>Exit Codes</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><code>0</code> - No violations or only warnings (if --fail-on=error)</li>
            <li><code>1</code> - Errors found (or warnings if --fail-on=warn)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Doctor Command</h2>
          <p>
            The <code>doctor</code> command runs diagnostics on your semicons installation.
          </p>

          <h3>Basic Usage</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli doctor</code></pre>

          <h3>Options</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Option</th>
                <th>Description</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>--fix</code></td>
                <td>Attempt automatic fixes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>--strict</code></td>
                <td>Treat warnings as errors</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <h3>Checks Performed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Config file existence and validity</li>
            <li>Theme configuration validity</li>
            <li>SVG file existence for local icons</li>
            <li>.gitignore configuration</li>
            <li>Registry completeness</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Example Output</h3>
          <pre><code>[doctor] Running diagnostics...
┌─────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┐
│ Code    │ Message                                │ Fix                    │
├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤
│ MISSING │ src/icons.generated/ not in .gitignore│ Add to .gitignore      │
│ _SVG    │                                        │                        │
└─────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘</code></pre>

          <h3>Auto-fix</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli doctor --fix</code></pre>
          <p>Automatically fixes common issues like .gitignore entries.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Strict Mode</h2>
          <p>
            Strict mode enforces additional validation rules and treats warnings as errors.
          </p>

          <h3>Enable Strict Mode</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli generate --strict</code></pre>

          <h3>Strict Mode Rules</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>All themes must be defined for each token</li>
            <li>Deprecated tokens produce errors instead of warnings</li>
            <li>Any normalization warning causes the command to fail</li>
            <li>Asset references are validated more strictly</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Use Cases</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>CI/CD pipelines</li>
            <li>Before releases</li>
            <li>Team code quality enforcement</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Theme Configuration</h2>
          <p>
            Themes allow you to define different icon variants for different contexts (light/dark mode, brand colors, etc.).
          </p>

          <h3>Configuration</h3>
          <pre><code>// semicons.config.mjs
export default &#123;
  version: '1.0.0',
  themes: ['light', 'dark', 'high-contrast'],
  defaultTheme: 'light',
  tokens: &#123;
    'navigation:menu': &#123;
      themes: &#123;
        light: 'local:menu-light',
        dark: 'local:menu-dark',
        'high-contrast': 'local:menu-contrast',
      &#125;,
    &#125;,
    'status:info': &#123;
      themes: &#123;
        light: 'local:info-blue',
        dark: 'local:info-blue',
        'high-contrast': 'local:info-white',
      &#125;,
    &#125;,
  &#125;,
&#125;;</code></pre>

          <h3>Theme Fallback</h3>
          <p>If a token doesn't define all themes, missing themes fall back to the default theme:</p>
          <pre><code>// This token only defines 'light', will fallback for dark
'status:success': &#123;
  themes: &#123;
    light: 'local:success-green',
  &#125;,
&#125;
// After generation:
themes: &#123;
  light: 'local:success-green',
  dark: 'local:success-green',  // fallback
&#125;</code></pre>

          <h3>Strict Theme Completeness</h3>
          <p>Use <code>--strict</code> to require all themes for every token:</p>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli generate --strict</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Configuration File</h2>
          <p>
            Semicons supports multiple configuration file formats and locations.
          </p>

          <h3>Supported File Names</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><code>semicons.config.mjs</code> (recommended)</li>
            <li><code>semicons.config.js</code></li>
            <li><code>semicons.config.json</code></li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Custom Config Path</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli generate --config path/to/config.mjs</code></pre>

          <h3>Example: MJS Config</h3>
          <pre><code>// semicons.config.mjs
export default &#123;
  version: '1.0.0',
  themes: ['light', 'dark'],
  defaultTheme: 'light',
  tokens: &#123;
    'navigation:menu': 'local:menu',
    'action:edit': 'local:edit',
    'status:error': 'local:error',
  &#125;,
&#125;;</code></pre>

          <h3>Example: JSON Config</h3>
          <pre><code>// semicons.config.json
&#123;
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "themes": ["light", "dark"],
  "defaultTheme": "light",
  "tokens": &#123;
    "navigation:menu": "local:menu"
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>SVG Optimization</h2>
          <p>
            The CLI uses SVGO to optimize SVG files during generation.
          </p>

          <h3>Skip Optimization</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli generate --no-optimize</code></pre>

          <h3>Custom SVGO Plugins</h3>
          <p>To customize optimization, create a custom SVGO config:</p>
          <pre><code>// svgo.config.js
export default &#123;
  multipass: true,
  plugins: [
    'preset-default',
    'removeDimensions',
    'convertStyleToAttrs',
  ],
&#125;;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Watch Mode</h2>
          <p>
            Watch mode automatically regenerates icons when configuration files or SVG files change.
            This is useful during development.
          </p>

          <h3>Basic Usage</h3>
          <pre><code>npx @semicons/cli generate --watch
# or
npx @semicons/cli generate -w</code></pre>

          <h3>Watched Files</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Configuration file (semicons.config.mjs/js/json)</li>
            <li>All SVG files in the icons directory</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Behavior</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Initial generation runs immediately</li>
            <li>Changes trigger regeneration after 300ms debounce</li>
            <li>Press <code>Ctrl+C</code> to stop watching</li>
            <li>Errors during regeneration are logged but don't stop the watcher</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Example Output</h3>
          <pre><code>$ npx @semicons/cli generate --watch

[generate:watch] Watching for changes...
[generate:watch] Config: semicons.config.mjs
[generate:watch] Output: src/icons.generated

[generate:watch] 2024-01-20T15:00:00.000Z - Regenerating...
[generate] Generating 10 tokens to src/icons.generated
[generate] Done!
[generate:watch] Watching for changes...

[generate:watch] File changed: icons/local/menu.svg
[generate:watch] 2024-01-20T15:01:00.000Z - Regenerating...
[generate] Generating 10 tokens to src/icons.generated
[generate] Done!
[generate:watch] Watching for changes...

^C
[generate:watch] Stopping watcher...</code></pre>

          <h3>Use Cases</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Development with hot reload</li>
            <li>Real-time icon preview</li>
            <li>Team collaboration on icon sets</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Generated Files</h2>
          <p>
            The <code>generate</code> command produces several files.
          </p>

          <h3>Output Structure</h3>
          <pre><code>src/icons.generated/
├── registry.json      # Icon registry (SSOT)
├── schema.json        # JSON Schema for validation
├── types.ts           # TypeScript types
├── types.d.ts         # TypeScript declarations
├── inline.ts          # Inline SVG data
├── inline.d.ts        # Inline SVG declarations
├── report.json        # Generation report
└── local/             # Optimized local SVG files
    ├── navigation-menu.light.svg
    └── navigation-menu.dark.svg

public/
└── semicons.svg       # SVG sprite sheet</code></pre>

          <h3>registry.json</h3>
          <pre><code>&#123;
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "themes": ["light", "dark"],
  "defaultTheme": "light",
  "tokens": [
    &#123;
      "name": "navigation:menu",
      "themes": &#123;
        "light": "local:menu-light",
        "dark": "local:menu-dark"
      &#125;,
      "a11y": &#123;
        "label": "Menu"
      &#125;,
      "meta": &#123;
        "category": "navigation"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>

          <h3>types.ts</h3>
          <pre><code>// Auto-generated by semicons
export type IconName = 'navigation:menu' | 'action:edit' | 'status:error';

export interface IconMeta &#123;
  name: string;
  category?: string;
  deprecated?: boolean | string;
  description?: string;
&#125;

export const ICON_META: Record&lt;IconName, IconMeta&gt; = &#123;
  'navigation:menu': &#123;
    name: 'navigation:menu',
    category: 'navigation',
  &#125;,
&#125;;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>CI/CD Integration</h2>
          <p>
            Integrate Semicons into your continuous integration pipeline.
          </p>

          <h3>GitHub Actions Example</h3>
          <pre><code># .github/workflows/icons.yml
name: Icons

on: [push, pull_request]

jobs:
  icons:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: pnpm/action-setup@v2
        with:
          version: '8'
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'pnpm'
      - run: pnpm install
      - run: pnpm semicons generate
      - run: pnpm semicons scan ./src --fail-on error
      - run: pnpm semicons doctor --strict</code></pre>

          <h3>Pre-commit Hook</h3>
          <pre><code># .pre-commit-config.yaml
- repo: local
  hooks:
    - id: semicons-generate
      name: Generate icons
      entry: pnpm semicons generate
      language: system
      pass_filenames: false
      stages: [pre-commit]</code></pre>
        </section>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
